// The wild ancestors of the first crops (v2 Era 3; V2-12): the wild wheats and barley of the
// Fertile Crescent's hills and the wild flax of the Mediterranean, each a stand one can strip of
// its grain in early summer, and a crop one can sow, tend and reap. A wild stand's ears shatter
// as they ripen and its seed lies dormant to sprout over several years; sown and reaped, and the
// best of its seed kept, a lot changes over the generations (`crop`).
